IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sfa-core`

-- Securities and Futures Act 2001 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation (a rendering, not the official text).
-- Layer 1, Part 8 (sections 138 to 140): the Securities Industry Council, the Take-over Code and the offences relating to take-over offers.
-- The Singapore Code on Take-overs and Mergers is NOT in this Act and is NOT encoded here: where a provision hands a matter to the Code or to the Council's rulings, the matter is an input.
-- Two functions answer the keel's seams: S1 (s 138(1), the Securities Industry Council) and S2 (s 139(2), the Take-over Code).

§ `s 138: the Securities Industry Council`

-- Seam S1: the keel's s 2(1) "Securities Industry Council" asks "the body is the Securities Industry Council referred to in section 138". This function is the answer, in section 138(1)'s own words.
-- src:31366 | 138.—(1) The advisory body known as the Securities Industry
-- src:31367 | Council referred to in section 14 of the repealed Securities Industry
-- src:31368 | Act (Cap. 289, 1985 Revised Edition) continues in existence as if it
-- src:31369 | had been established under this Act.
@ref s 138(1) (src:31366-31369)
GIVEN
    `the body is the advisory body known as the Securities Industry Council referred to in section 14 of the repealed Securities Industry Act (Cap. 289, 1985 Revised Edition)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body the advisory body known as the Securities Industry Council referred to in section 14 of the repealed Securities Industry Act (Cap. 289, 1985 Revised Edition)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 138(1) the body is the Securities Industry Council referred to in section 138` MEANS
    IF `the body is the advisory body known as the Securities Industry Council referred to in section 14 of the repealed Securities Industry Act (Cap. 289, 1985 Revised Edition)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The advisory body known as the Securities Industry Council referred to in section 14 of the repealed Securities Industry Act" "continues in existence as if it had been established under this Act"; another body is not mentioned

-- src:31371 | (2) The function of the Securities Industry Council is, in addition to
-- src:31372 | the functions conferred upon it under this Part, to advise the Minister
-- src:31373 | on all matters relating to the securities industry.
@ref s 138(2) (src:31371-31373)
GIVEN
    `the matter relates to the securities industry` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the matter relate to the securities industry?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 138(2) the Securities Industry Council has the function of advising the Minister on the matter` MEANS
    IF `the matter relates to the securities industry`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to advise the Minister on all matters relating to the securities industry"; a matter that does not relate to the securities industry is not mentioned

-- src:31375 | (3) The Securities Industry Council consists of such representatives
-- src:31376 | of business, the Government and the Authority as the Minister may
-- src:31377 | appoint and those representatives are to serve for such period or
-- src:31378 | periods as the Minister may determine.
@ref s 138(3) (src:31375-31378)
GIVEN
    `the person is a representative of business, the Government or the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a representative of business, the Government or the Authority?
    `the Minister has appointed the person to the Securities Industry Council` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister appointed the person to the Securities Industry Council?
    `the day falls within a period the Minister has determined for the person to serve` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the day fall within a period that the Minister has determined for the person to serve on the Securities Industry Council?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 138(3) the person serves on the Securities Industry Council` MEANS
    IF `the person is a representative of business, the Government or the Authority` AND `the Minister has appointed the person to the Securities Industry Council` AND `the day falls within a period the Minister has determined for the person to serve`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "such representatives of business, the Government and the Authority as the Minister may appoint" "to serve for such period or periods as the Minister may determine"; the appointment and the period are the Minister's acts

-- Subsection (4): the Council's power to enquire and to summon. "for this purpose" and "necessary for the purpose of the enquiry" limit the power in its own wording.
-- src:31380 | (4) The Securities Industry Council has the power, in the exercise of
-- src:31381 | its functions, to enquire into any matter or thing related to the
-- src:31382 | securities industry and may, for this purpose, summon any person to
-- src:31383 | give evidence on oath or affirmation or produce any document or
-- src:31384 | material necessary for the purpose of the enquiry.
@ref s 138(4) (src:31380-31384)
GIVEN
    `the Securities Industry Council is exercising its functions in an enquiry into a matter or thing related to the securities industry` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Securities Industry Council, in the exercise of its functions, enquiring into a matter or thing related to the securities industry?
    `the evidence, document or material is necessary for the purpose of the enquiry` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the evidence, document or material necessary for the purpose of the enquiry?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 138(4) the Securities Industry Council may summon the person to give evidence on oath or affirmation or produce a document or material` MEANS
    IF `the Securities Industry Council is exercising its functions in an enquiry into a matter or thing related to the securities industry` AND `the evidence, document or material is necessary for the purpose of the enquiry`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in the exercise of its functions, to enquire into any matter or thing related to the securities industry and may, for this purpose, summon any person" "necessary for the purpose of the enquiry"

-- Subsection (5) is a flat negative ("Nothing in subsection (4) compels"). For the advocate and solicitor, or legal counsel, who holds a document containing a privileged communication,
-- the answer to "is the document protected from production under subsection (4)?" is JUST TRUE; for anyone else subsection (5) is silent, so NOTHING.
-- src:31386 | (5) Nothing in subsection (4) compels the production by an
-- src:31387 | advocate and solicitor, or a legal counsel referred to in
-- src:31388 | section 128A of the Evidence Act 1893, of a document containing
-- src:31389 | a privileged communication made by or to him or her in that capacity
-- src:31390 | or authorise the taking of possession of any such document which is
-- src:31391 | in his or her possession.
@ref s 138(5) (src:31386-31391)
GIVEN
    `the person is an advocate and solicitor, or a legal counsel referred to in section 128A of the Evidence Act 1893` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an advocate and solicitor, or a legal counsel referred to in section 128A of the Evidence Act 1893?
    `the document contains a privileged communication made by or to the person in that capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the document contain a privileged communication made by or to the person in that capacity (as advocate and solicitor, or legal counsel)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 138(5) the document is protected from production and from the taking of possession under subsection (4)` MEANS
    IF `the person is an advocate and solicitor, or a legal counsel referred to in section 128A of the Evidence Act 1893` AND `the document contains a privileged communication made by or to the person in that capacity`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Nothing in subsection (4) compels the production by an advocate and solicitor, or a legal counsel referred to in section 128A of the Evidence Act 1893, of a document containing a privileged communication made by or to him or her in that capacity"

-- Subsection (6): the lawyer who refuses to produce is nevertheless obliged to give the name and address "(if he or she knows them)". The duty is the provision's own question.
-- A lawyer who refuses and does not know them: the parenthesis says the duty is limited to what the lawyer knows, so JUST FALSE (marginal reading (a): a failed "if" counted as the text's no; the other reading is NOTHING).
-- Anyone who is not a lawyer refusing to produce the document is outside the sentence: NOTHING.
-- src:31398 | (6) An advocate and solicitor, or a legal counsel referred to in
-- src:31399 | section 128A of the Evidence Act 1893, who refuses to produce the
-- src:31400 | document referred to in subsection (5) is nevertheless obliged to give
-- src:31401 | the name and address (if he or she knows them) of the person to
-- src:31402 | whom or by or on behalf of whom the communication was made.
@ref s 138(6) (src:31398-31402)
GIVEN
    `the person is an advocate and solicitor, or a legal counsel referred to in section 128A of the Evidence Act 1893` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an advocate and solicitor, or a legal counsel referred to in section 128A of the Evidence Act 1893?
    `the person refuses to produce the document referred to in section 138(5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person refuse to produce the document referred to in section 138(5)?
    `the person knows the name and address of the person to whom or by or on behalf of whom the communication was made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person know the name and address of the person to whom or by or on behalf of whom the communication was made?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 138(6) the person must give the name and address of the person to whom or by or on behalf of whom the communication was made` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT (`the person is an advocate and solicitor, or a legal counsel referred to in section 128A of the Evidence Act 1893` AND `the person refuses to produce the document referred to in section 138(5)`))
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An advocate and solicitor, or a legal counsel referred to in section 128A of the Evidence Act 1893, who refuses to produce the document referred to in subsection (5) is nevertheless obliged"
        IF `the person knows the name and address of the person to whom or by or on behalf of whom the communication was made`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the name and address (if he or she knows them)"
        -- MARGINAL-READING (a): the duty is introduced with "if he or she knows them"; a failed "if" is taken as the text's no. The other reading is NOTHING.

DECLARE `s 138 action` IS ONE OF
    `s 138 give the name and address of the person to whom or by or on behalf of whom the communication was made`

-- "is nevertheless obliged to give" is a MUST with no time limit and no stated consequence, so no trace can show it breached (NOTES.md, "Rules with no breach path").
-- src:31398 | (6) An advocate and solicitor, or a legal counsel referred to in
-- src:31399 | section 128A of the Evidence Act 1893, who refuses to produce the
-- src:31400 | document referred to in subsection (5) is nevertheless obliged to give
-- src:31401 | the name and address (if he or she knows them) of the person to
-- src:31402 | whom or by or on behalf of whom the communication was made.
@ref s 138(6) (the duty as a regulative rule) (src:31398-31402)
GIVEN `the person` IS A Party
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 138 action`
`s 138(6) the lawyer must give the name and address` MEANS
    PARTY `the person`
    MUST `s 138 give the name and address of the person to whom or by or on behalf of whom the communication was made`
    HENCE FULFILLED

