-- Subsection (10): "Subject to the provisions of this Act". Where a provision of the Act provides otherwise the answer is that provision's: it points outside this section.
-- src:31425 | (10) Subject to the provisions of this Act, the Securities Industry
-- src:31426 | Council may regulate its own procedure and is not bound by the rules
-- src:31427 | of evidence.
@ref s 138(10) (src:31425-31427)
GIVEN
    `a provision of the Act provides otherwise for the procedure of the Securities Industry Council or the rules of evidence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a provision of the Act provide otherwise for the procedure of the Securities Industry Council or for the rules of evidence?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 138(10) the Securities Industry Council may regulate its own procedure and is not bound by the rules of evidence` MEANS
    IF (NOT `a provision of the Act provides otherwise for the procedure of the Securities Industry Council or the rules of evidence`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Subject to the provisions of this Act"; the provision that provides otherwise decides

§ `s 139: the Take-over Code`

-- src:31431 | 139.—(1) This section and section 140 apply to and in relation to all
-- src:31432 | natural persons, whether resident in Singapore or not and whether
-- src:31433 | citizens of Singapore or not, and to all corporations or bodies
-- src:31434 | unincorporate, whether incorporated or carrying on business in
-- src:31435 | Singapore or not, and extend to acts done outside Singapore.
@ref s 139(1) (src:31431-31435)
GIVEN
    `the person is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an individual (a natural person)?
    `the person is a corporation or body unincorporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a corporation or a body unincorporate?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 139(1) sections 139 and 140 apply to the person and extend to acts done outside Singapore` MEANS
    IF `the person is an individual` OR `the person is a corporation or body unincorporate`
    THEN JUST TRUE  -- "whether resident in Singapore or not and whether citizens of Singapore or not" and "whether incorporated or carrying on business in Singapore or not": residence, citizenship and place of business make no difference, so none is an input
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "all natural persons" and "all corporations or bodies unincorporate"; another kind of person is not mentioned

-- Seam S2: the keel's s 2(1) "Take-over Code" asks "the document is the Singapore Code on Take-overs and Mergers referred to in section 139 and issued by the Authority under section 321(1)".
-- This function is the answer, in section 139(2)'s own words; "called in this Act the Take-over Code" is a label, and section 321 (a later wave) is an input.
-- src:31437 | (2) For the more effective administration, supervision and control
-- src:31438 | of take‑over offers and matters connected therewith, the Authority is
-- src:31439 | to, on the advice of the Securities Industry Council and under
