    `the document is the code known as the Singapore Code on Take-overs and Mergers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document the code known as the Singapore Code on Take-overs and Mergers?
    `the Authority issued the document on the advice of the Securities Industry Council and under section 321` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Authority issue the document on the advice of the Securities Industry Council and under section 321?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 139(2) the document is the Singapore Code on Take-overs and Mergers referred to in section 139 and issued by the Authority under section 321(1)` MEANS
    IF `the document is the code known as the Singapore Code on Take-overs and Mergers` AND `the Authority issued the document on the advice of the Securities Industry Council and under section 321`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "issue a code known as the Singapore Code on Take-overs and Mergers (called in this Act the Take-over Code)"; another document is not mentioned

