-- Subsection (8): a flat negative ("does not of itself render that party liable to criminal proceedings"). The text's no, in its own words, for a failure to observe the Code taken alone.
-- src:31466 | (8) A failure of any party concerned in a take‑over offer or a matter
-- src:31467 | connected therewith to observe any of the provisions of the Take‑over
-- src:31468 | Code does not of itself render that party liable to criminal proceedings
-- src:31469 | but any such failure may, in any proceedings whether civil or
@ref s 139(8) (no criminal liability of itself) (src:31466-31469)
GIVEN
    `the party has failed to observe a provision of the Take-over Code` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the party concerned in a take-over offer or a matter connected with one failed to observe a provision of the Take-over Code?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 139(8) the failure of itself renders the party liable to criminal proceedings` MEANS
    IF `the party has failed to observe a provision of the Take-over Code`
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not of itself render that party liable to criminal proceedings"
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A failure of any party concerned in a take-over offer or a matter connected therewith to observe any of the provisions of the Take-over Code"; no failure is not mentioned

-- src:31469 | but any such failure may, in any proceedings whether civil or
-- src:31470 | criminal, be relied upon by any party to the proceedings as tending to
-- src:31471 | establish or to negate any liability which is in question in the
-- src:31472 | proceedings.
@ref s 139(8) (reliance in proceedings) (src:31469-31472)
GIVEN
    `the party has failed to observe a provision of the Take-over Code` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the party concerned in a take-over offer or a matter connected with one failed to observe a provision of the Take-over Code?
    `the failure is relied upon in proceedings, civil or criminal, as tending to establish or to negate a liability in question in them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the failure relied upon, in proceedings (civil or criminal), as tending to establish or to negate a liability that is in question in them?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 139(8) the failure may be relied upon in proceedings as tending to establish or to negate a liability` MEANS
    IF `the party has failed to observe a provision of the Take-over Code` AND `the failure is relied upon in proceedings, civil or criminal, as tending to establish or to negate a liability in question in them`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any such failure may, in any proceedings whether civil or criminal, be relied upon by any party to the proceedings as tending to establish or to negate any liability which is in question in the proceedings"

-- Subsection (9): "Nothing in subsection (8) is to be construed as preventing" the Council from invoking sanctions, including public censure.
-- src:31474 | (9) Nothing in subsection (8) is to be construed as preventing the
-- src:31475 | Securities Industry Council from invoking such sanctions (including
-- src:31476 | public censure) as it may decide in relation to breaches of the
-- src:31477 | Take‑over Code by any party concerned in a take‑over offer or a
-- src:31478 | matter connected therewith.
@ref s 139(9) (src:31474-31478)
GIVEN
    `the sanction is one the Securities Industry Council decides to invoke for a breach of the Take-over Code by a party concerned` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the sanction (including public censure) one that the Securities Industry Council decides to invoke in relation to a breach of the Take-over Code by a party concerned in a take-over offer or a matter connected with one?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 139(9) subsection (8) does not prevent the Securities Industry Council from invoking the sanction` MEANS
    IF `the sanction is one the Securities Industry Council decides to invoke for a breach of the Take-over Code by a party concerned`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "such sanctions (including public censure) as it may decide in relation to breaches of the Take-over Code by any party concerned in a take-over offer or a matter connected therewith"

-- Subsection (10): "Where the Securities Industry Council has reason to believe ... the Securities Industry Council has power to enquire". A power gated by "Where": SPLIT-SITE (ii), fork line B15.
-- src:31480 | (10) Where the Securities Industry Council has reason to believe
-- src:31481 | that any party concerned in a take‑over offer or a matter connected
-- src:31482 | therewith, or any person advising on a take‑over offer or a matter
-- src:31483 | connected therewith, is in breach of the provisions of the Take‑over
-- src:31484 | Code or is otherwise believed to have committed acts of misconduct
-- src:31485 | in relation to such take‑over offer or matter, the Securities Industry
-- src:31486 | Council has power to enquire into the suspected breach or
-- src:31487 | misconduct.
@ref s 139(10) (src:31480-31487)
GIVEN
    `the Securities Industry Council has reason to believe that the person is in breach of the Take-over Code or has committed acts of misconduct in relation to the offer or matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Securities Industry Council have reason to believe that the person is in breach of the Take-over Code, or is otherwise believed to have committed acts of misconduct, in relation to the take-over offer or matter?
    `the person is a party concerned in a take-over offer or a matter connected with one, or a person advising on one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a party concerned in a take-over offer or a matter connected with one, or a person advising on a take-over offer or a matter connected with one?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 139(10) the Securities Industry Council has power to enquire into the suspected breach or misconduct` MEANS
    IF `the Securities Industry Council has reason to believe that the person is in breach of the Take-over Code or has committed acts of misconduct in relation to the offer or matter` AND `the person is a party concerned in a take-over offer or a matter connected with one, or a person advising on one`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): SPLIT-SITE (ii) "Where the Securities Industry Council has reason to believe that any party concerned in a take-over offer or a matter connected therewith, or any person advising on a take-over offer or a matter connected therewith" "the Securities Industry Council has power to enquire into the suspected breach or misconduct"

-- src:31492 | (11) For the purpose of subsection (10), the Securities Industry
-- src:31493 | Council may summon any person to give evidence on oath or
-- src:31494 | affirmation, which it is authorised to administer, or produce any
-- src:31495 | document or material necessary for the purpose of the enquiry.
@ref s 139(11) (src:31492-31495)
GIVEN
    `the Securities Industry Council is enquiring into a suspected breach or misconduct under section 139(10)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Securities Industry Council enquiring into a suspected breach or misconduct under section 139(10)?
    `the evidence, document or material is necessary for the purpose of the enquiry` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the evidence, document or material necessary for the purpose of the enquiry?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 139(11) the Securities Industry Council may summon the person to give evidence on oath or affirmation or produce a document or material` MEANS
    IF `the Securities Industry Council is enquiring into a suspected breach or misconduct under section 139(10)` AND `the evidence, document or material is necessary for the purpose of the enquiry`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For the purpose of subsection (10)" "necessary for the purpose of the enquiry"

§ `s 140: offences relating to take-over offers`

-- Subsection (1): "A person who has no intention to make an offer in the nature of a take-over offer must not give notice or publicly announce that the person intends to make a take-over offer."
-- The prohibition is limited by its class ("who has no intention"): the case outside the class is NOTHING (the Guide's "limits a grant or prohibition in its own wording and the case falls outside the limit").
-- src:31499 | 140.—(1) A person who has no intention to make an offer in the
-- src:31500 | nature of a take‑over offer must not give notice or publicly announce
-- src:31501 | that the person intends to make a take‑over offer.
@ref s 140(1) (src:31499-31501)
GIVEN
    `the person has no intention to make an offer in the nature of a take-over offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person have no intention to make an offer in the nature of a take-over offer?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 140(1) the person must not give notice or publicly announce that the person intends to make a take-over offer` MEANS
    IF `the person has no intention to make an offer in the nature of a take-over offer`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who has no intention to make an offer in the nature of a take-over offer must not give notice or publicly announce that the person intends to make a take-over offer"

-- src:31503 | (2) A person must not make a take‑over offer or give notice or
-- src:31504 | publicly announce that the person intends to make a take‑over offer if
-- src:31505 | the person has no reasonable or probable grounds for believing that
-- src:31506 | the person will be able to perform the person’s obligations if the
-- src:31507 | take‑over offer is accepted or approved, as the case may be.
@ref s 140(2) (src:31503-31507)
GIVEN
    `the person has no reasonable or probable grounds for believing that the person will be able to perform the person's obligations if the take-over offer is accepted or approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person have no reasonable or probable grounds for believing that the person will be able to perform the person's obligations if the take-over offer is accepted or approved, as the case may be?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 140(2) the person must not make a take-over offer or give notice or publicly announce that the person intends to make one` MEANS
    IF `the person has no reasonable or probable grounds for believing that the person will be able to perform the person's obligations if the take-over offer is accepted or approved`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the person has no reasonable or probable grounds for believing that the person will be able to perform the person's obligations if the take-over offer is accepted or approved, as the case may be"

DECLARE `s 140 action` IS ONE OF
    `s 140(1) give notice or publicly announce that the person intends to make a take-over offer`
    `s 140(2) make a take-over offer, or give notice or publicly announce that the person intends to make one`

-- The two prohibitions as regulative rules (SHANT, derived from the flat negative "must not": ruling N2 of 2026-11-04), so that a trace can reach the offence of subsection (3).
-- The rule's Party is the person in the class the subsection names (one with no intention; one with no reasonable or probable grounds).
-- src:31499 | 140.—(1) A person who has no intention to make an offer in the
-- src:31500 | nature of a take‑over offer must not give notice or publicly announce
-- src:31501 | that the person intends to make a take‑over offer.
@ref s 140(1) (the prohibition as a regulative rule) (src:31499-31501)
GIVEN `the person` IS A Party
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 140 action`
`s 140(1) the person with no intention shall not give notice or publicly announce an intention to make a take-over offer` MEANS
    PARTY `the person`
    SHANT `s 140(1) give notice or publicly announce that the person intends to make a take-over offer`
    LEST BREACH BY `the person` BECAUSE "gave notice or publicly announced an intention to make a take-over offer with no intention to make an offer in the nature of a take-over offer (section 140(1)): an offence under section 140(3)"

-- src:31503 | (2) A person must not make a take‑over offer or give notice or
-- src:31504 | publicly announce that the person intends to make a take‑over offer if
-- src:31505 | the person has no reasonable or probable grounds for believing that
-- src:31506 | the person will be able to perform the person’s obligations if the
-- src:31507 | take‑over offer is accepted or approved, as the case may be.
@ref s 140(2) (the prohibition as a regulative rule) (src:31503-31507)
GIVEN `the person` IS A Party
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 140 action`
`s 140(2) the person with no grounds shall not make a take-over offer or announce an intention to make one` MEANS
    PARTY `the person`
    SHANT `s 140(2) make a take-over offer, or give notice or publicly announce that the person intends to make one`
    LEST BREACH BY `the person` BECAUSE "made a take-over offer, or gave notice or publicly announced an intention to make one, with no reasonable or probable grounds for believing that the person could perform the obligations (section 140(2)): an offence under section 140(3)"

-- Subsection (3): the offence, for the person, and for the corporation's officer in default. An unmet element is NOTHING: SPLIT-SITE (i), fork line B16.
-- src:31509 | (3) Where a person contravenes subsection (1) or (2), the person
-- src:31510 | and, where the person is a corporation, every officer of the
-- src:31511 | corporation who is in default shall be guilty of an offence and shall
-- src:31512 | be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $250,000 or to
-- src:31513 | imprisonment for a term not exceeding 7 years or to both.
@ref s 140(3) (the person) (src:31509-31513)
GIVEN
    `the person contravenes section 140(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person contravene section 140(1)?
    `the person contravenes section 140(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person contravene section 140(2)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 140(3) the person is guilty of an offence under section 140` MEANS
    IF `the person contravenes section 140(1)` OR `the person contravenes section 140(2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): SPLIT-SITE (i) the text says who is guilty ("Where a person contravenes subsection (1) or (2), the person"), not that a person who does not is innocent

-- src:31509 | (3) Where a person contravenes subsection (1) or (2), the person
-- src:31510 | and, where the person is a corporation, every officer of the
-- src:31511 | corporation who is in default shall be guilty of an offence and shall
-- src:31512 | be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $250,000 or to
-- src:31513 | imprisonment for a term not exceeding 7 years or to both.
@ref s 140(3) (the officer in default) (src:31509-31513)
GIVEN
    `the person is a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a corporation (as section 2(1) defines "corporation")?
    `the person contravenes section 140(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person contravene section 140(1)?
    `the person contravenes section 140(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person contravene section 140(2)?
    `the officer of the corporation is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the officer of the corporation in default?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 140(3) the officer of the corporation is guilty of an offence under section 140` MEANS
    IF `the person is a corporation` AND (`the person contravenes section 140(1)` OR `the person contravenes section 140(2)`) AND `the officer of the corporation is in default`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): SPLIT-SITE (i) the text says who is guilty ("where the person is a corporation, every officer of the corporation who is in default"), not that an officer not in default is innocent

-- src:31509 | (3) Where a person contravenes subsection (1) or (2), the person
-- src:31510 | and, where the person is a corporation, every officer of the
-- src:31511 | corporation who is in default shall be guilty of an offence and shall
-- src:31512 | be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $250,000 or to
-- src:31513 | imprisonment for a term not exceeding 7 years or to both.
@ref 2 s 140(3) (the penalty) (src:31509-31513)
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 140(3) the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    -- a fine not exceeding $250,000 or imprisonment for a term not exceeding 7 years (84 months) or both; no daily fine is stated, so 0
    Penalty OF 250000, 84, TRUE, 0
